;;; A query's `:goal` whose `(absent …)` writes a pattern inside a pattern with
;;; a variable as its relation loads, and holds in every state — **W79**,
;;; register row `W79/goal-absent-nested-relation-variable`.
;;;
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `goal-nested-relation-variable.ein` with its goal negated: `(absent (says (?R
;;; ?g)))`, nothing is said.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Refused at load, as the pattern is without the `(absent …)`, one line, on every
;;; command (exit 1, `ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `73a0c17d`, release: the program loads, the inner pattern matches
;;; nothing, so the `(absent …)` holds, and the read-out answers *the goal
;;; holds* beside `(says (paid Bob))`, exit 0 on every command. Now refused at
;;; load.

(relation says Guest :why "{?1} says something")
(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(says (paid Bob))
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (absent (says (?R ?g))))
